The College of Engineering and Information Technology (CEIT) is a premier academic department within Kalinga State University (KSU), located in Bulanao, Tabuk City, Kalinga. The college is dedicated to providing quality education, technical proficiency, and innovative training to students pursuing careers in engineering, computer science, and information technology.

CEIT plays a vital role in fulfilling the university's mandate to produce competent professionals who can contribute to the technological and infrastructural development of the region and the country. The college manages multiple degree programs, requiring the rigorous administration of student academic records, faculty performance metrics, course curricula, and technical training documentation.

The college administration is spearheaded by the Dean, supported by Program Chairpersons, faculty members, and administrative support staff. These personnel are collectively responsible for maintaining the academic standards of the college, ensuring compliance with CHED regulations, and preparing the department for rigorous AACCUP accreditation evaluations. The college relies heavily on the accurate and timely processing of records to manage student progress, evaluate faculty, and make data-driven administrative decisions.

The proposed E-records system is directly related to the operations of CEIT, as it seeks to modernize and secure the very core of its administrative workflow, providing the college with the technological infrastructure necessary to manage its growing repository of academic data efficiently.